{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/3554-endowment-idea","id":3554,"title":"Endowment idea","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-05T09:10:29-08:00","id":3554,"title":"Endowment idea","content":"Okay, I'm sure that several versions of this idea have been done before, but here's my thought. It could either be an endowment for a NEW conspiracy, an endowment for The Long Night upgraded to conspiracy level, or an alternate endowment for the Maleus.<br /> <br /> <br /> Short Summary: Faith is bonus Willpower, and also a Power Trait.<br /> <br /> <br /> Faith (* to *****)<br /> Each Dot of Faith also provides provides temporary points of Faith, which can be spent exactly the same way as willpower. Faith can be restored in two ways. 1&gt; If you fulfill your virtue in a short term manner (much like fulfilling your Vice for willpower) once per scene you can regain a spent Faith. 2&gt; Once per story, when you fulfill your Virtue in a manner that would grant you a total willpower refresh, you can choose INSTEAD to fully refill your Faith (this is an either/or situation, if you use your virtue to refill you Willpower you can't use it to full refill your faith this session, and vice versa).<br /> <br /> Spending Faith does not count towards you limit of spending willpower.<br /> <br /> Finally, Faith counts as a supernatural power trait. Any power that allows a character to add a power trait like Blood Potency, Azoth, or Sekhem to resist, the hunter can add his Faith score to his resistance.<br /> <br /> Faith 1-2, can spend 1 Faith per turn<br /> Faith 3-4, can spend 2 Faith per turn<br /> Faith 5, can spend 3 Faith per turn<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T14:57:31-08:00","id":3781,"title":"","content":"The endowment for the long night is already better than this: They regain every day with prayer, they can use it ignore wound penalties, and they can gift willpower to others as well as refilling willpower with it or as a supernatural resistance trait (against mental attacks). Being able to replenish 6 willpower every day with sleep and daily prayer is a big big benefit.<br /> <br /> It's an underwhelming alternative to the magics of the inquisition.<br /> <br /> Do you have mirrors? You're proposal is a lot like Conviction, from that book, which if you use that option every mortal gets for free at one point, so you can have hunters with a supernatural resistance trait without using up their endowment slot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T17:00:07-08:00","id":14379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/3554-endowment-idea?p=3781#post3781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have mirrors? You're proposal is a lot like Conviction, from that book, which if you use that option every mortal gets for free at one point, so you can have hunters with a supernatural resistance trait without using up their endowment slot.</div> </div> </div> </div>May seem like a dumb question, but what do you mean when you say mirrors? Is that a rulebook? Only ask because I'm not familiar with it and I thought I had the complete nWoD collection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/19.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1220-carnivalcash","name":"CarnivalCash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T17:25:34-08:00","id":14393,"title":"","content":"Mirrors is a World of Darkness supplement that basically says &quot;Hey, you know all those rules and ideas you've been playing with for years? What if we just said fuck them all and gave you whole new ones?&quot;. Mirrors provides a smorgasbord of reinvented rules, systems, and settings for the World of Darkness, and is probably the best supplement for the game bar none, go grab it now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T02:09:25-08:00","id":14601,"title":"","content":"There are three Mirrors books. The book just called Mirrors at 227 pages, and two Mirrors setting shard pdfs at ~25 pages each.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/82477/World-of-Darkness-Mirrors\" target=\"_blank\">Mirrors</a> -- A bunch of hacks, shards (alternate settings) and templates for things like generic magic systems and heroic/extraordinary mortals.<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/87936/Mirrors-Bleeding-Edge\" target=\"_blank\">Mirrors: Bleeding Edge</a> -- A setting shard wherein the World of Darkness is a science fiction cyberpunk dystopia of digital realities and cybernetic implants..<br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/87937/Mirrors-Infinite-Macabre\" target=\"_blank\">Mirrors: Infinite Macabre</a> -- The World of Darkness in SPAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACE.<br /> <br /> Mirrors is one of the best additions to the World of Darkness ever made, and lacking it in ones collection is a terrible mistake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/508-sikker","name":"sikker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T01:29:48-08:00","id":15232,"title":"","content":"Yes, thirded, I figure the only reason not to get the book is either you're perfectly happy with every single rule in the nwod system, or you're one of those guys who would gladly build your own homebrew anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}